# Returns and Refund Policy for E-commerce Support

This sample policy describes buyer return and refund handling for an e-commerce support RAG lab. Buyers may request return or refund support when an order is not received, arrives damaged, is missing items, or is materially different from the listing description. The buyer should submit the request within the platform dispute window and provide clear evidence such as photos, unboxing video, delivery tracking status, chat history, and payment receipt.

The support team reviews whether the item is eligible for return, whether the seller has provided sufficient response, and whether the logistics record confirms delivery. Refunds may be issued to the original payment method or to platform wallet balance depending on payment route and marketplace policy. The buyer must keep the item and packaging until the dispute is resolved.

Sellers must respond to return requests within the required service timeline. If the seller does not respond, the platform may decide using buyer evidence and logistics data. Returned items should be sent using the platform-approved shipping method when required. The policy protects buyers from defective products while giving sellers a chance to provide proof of correct fulfillment.

Common support questions include how to request a return, what evidence is needed for a refund request, how long refund review takes, and what happens when the seller rejects a claim. This document is intentionally long enough for conversion, chunking, retrieval, BM25 keyword search, semantic search, RRF reranking, and citation generation tests.
